.TH ADDR2LINE 1 "March 2026" "Substrate" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
addr2line \- convert addresses to file names and line numbers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B addr2line
[\fIOPTION\fR]... [\fIADDRESS\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B addr2line
translates program addresses into source locations using DWARF debug data.
By default it reads from
.I a.out
and prints one
.IR file:line
result per query.
.PP
If no addresses are provided on the command line, addresses are read from
standard input, one per line.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-e " FILE\fR,\fP " \-\-exe= FILE
Use
.I FILE
as the input ELF object (default:
.IR a.out ).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-functions
Print function names before source locations.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-inlines
Print inline call frames from innermost to outermost.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-basenames
Strip directory prefixes from file names.
.TP
.BI \-j " SECTION\fR,\fP " \-\-section= SECTION
Treat input addresses as offsets in
.IR SECTION .
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-demangle
Demangle function names using
.BR demangle (3).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pretty\-print
Print each frame on one line as
.IR "function at file:line" .
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-addresses
Print the queried address before each result.
.TP
.B \-c
Print
.IR file:line:column
when column data is available.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit with status 0.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit with status 0.
.SH OUTPUT
If a lookup fails,
.B addr2line
prints:
.PP
.RS
??
.br
??:0
.RE
.PP
with
.B \-f
enabled, or just:
.PP
.RS
??:0
.RE
.PP
without
.BR \-f .
.SH ADDRESS ADJUSTMENT
For
.B ET_DYN
objects (PIE and shared libraries),
.B addr2line
applies load-bias style correction when absolute runtime addresses are given.
.SH DWARF SUPPORT
Supported DWARF versions: v2, v3, v4, v5.
.PP
Supported compressed debug formats:
.I .zdebug_*
(GNU zlib)
and
.I SHF_COMPRESSED
debug sections.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (including unresolved addresses).
.TP
.B 1
Fatal error, such as invalid ELF format, unreadable input file, or bad options.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Resolve two addresses from an executable:
.PP
.RS
.EX
addr2line -e ./kernel.elf 0x8049123 0x8049567
.EE
.RE
.TP
Resolve runtime-style PIE addresses with function names:
.PP
.RS
.EX
addr2line -f -e ./app.pie 0x555551a3 0x5555520f
.EE
.RE
.TP
Read addresses from standard input:
.PP
.RS
.EX
printf '0x401050\\n0x401080\\n' | addr2line -e ./a.out
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR demangle (3),
.BR c++filt (1),
.BR nm (1),
.BR objdump (1),
.BR readelf (1)
